Tibetan Buddhism is based on the teachings of Gautama Buddha, but it has expanded through the Mahayana sect's path of compassion and numerous techniques from Indian yoga.
Essentially, Tibetan Buddhism is very simple. It consists of the path that fully embraces kundalini yoga, meditation, and love.
Kundalini, the state of yoga, is awakened through yoga, breath exercises, mantras, and visualizations, activating kundalini energy (the energy of enlightenment).
The central focus of Tibetan meditation is deity yoga. The energy channels become cleared through the visualization of various deities, the chakras become activated, and enlightened awareness arises.
