AI systems are currently widely used in fields such as economics, medicine, engineering, and the military, including the development of numerous home computer and video game software applications.
Field trips constitute a significant part of any classroom experience. Often, a teacher would want to take her students to places where travel by bus is not an option.
Technology provides a solution through virtual field trips. Students can view rare museum specimens, tour aquaria, or appreciate beautiful artworks while sitting in their classrooms.
Participation in the virtual world field trip is an excellent way to reflect on this trip and contribute experiences to future classes.
For example, each year students at the Bennett School in Northern Kiro Lina design a website for their journey to the state capital. Each year the website is rebuilt from scratch, but older versions are kept online to serve as an archive.
Blogs can also improve students' writing skills. Students begin their blogging with errors in grammar and spelling, but ultimately, the community of blog readers corrects these mistakes.
Since students are generally critical, the blogger strives to improve his writing in order to avoid criticism.
Blogging also "compels students to become more aware of their immediate world." The need to generate interest among readers (listeners) encourages students to be alert and engaging (Toto, 2004).
Blogging is a tool that encourages collaboration and promotes better learning skills beyond traditional school days.
Appropriate use of blogs can help students become more analytical and critical, enabling them to actively utilize online content, position themselves in relation to others' writings, and outline their own perspectives on specific issues (O'Neil, 2002).
