Kruger National Park (KNP) is located in northeastern South Africa, stretching from the border with Mozambique in the east to Zimbabwe in the north and the Limpopo River in the south.
This park covers an area of 19,500 square kilometers and is divided into 14 distinct ecological zones, each of which is conducive to a different type of wildlife.
It is one of the most fundamental and attractive places in South Africa, and is regarded as one of the most important features of South African National Parks (SAN Parks).
Like all South African national parks, this park also has a daily conservation and entry fee.
It could also be beneficial for anyone looking to purchase a wildcard, which provides entry to selected parks in South Africa or all of South Africa's national parks.
The region of Hong Kong is named after the island of Hong Kong, and it is the place that many tourists consider as their center for tourism.
The rows of buildings that make up Hong Kong's skyline now form a glowing bar chart, clearly visible in the waters of Victoria Harbour.
Leave the island to get the best view of Hong Kong, and go to the waterfront opposite, Colombo Waterfront.
A large number of Hong Kong Island's urban constructions are concentrated on the available land along the northern coast.
This is the place that the British imperialists turned into their own, and similarly, if you are looking for evidence of the region's colonial past, this is a good place to begin.
Sundarbans is the world's largest coastal mangrove belt, stretching 80 kilometers (50 miles) from the coastal areas into the remote, underdeveloped regions of Bangladesh and India.
Sundarbans has been designated a UNESCO World Heritage site. The portion of the forest located in the Indian region is known as Sundarbans National Park.
Forests are not merely mangrove swamps—they include some remaining strips of great forests that once covered the Gangetic plains.
Sundarbans covers an area of 3,850 km², one-third of which consists of water/swampy regions.
Since 1966, Sundarbans has been a wildlife sanctuary, and it is estimated that the area now has about 400 Bengal tigers and nearly 30,000 spotted deer.
