During other times of the year, one can also witness tournaments and matches of lower grade here.
For information on news related to the tournament and where to buy tickets for polo matches, check the Association Argentina de Polo.
The official currency of the Falkland Islands is the Falkland Islands pound (FKP), which is pegged at par with the British pound (GBP).
Currency exchange is available only at the island's single bank, located in Stanley, in front of the F.I. C. West Store.
British pounds are generally accepted anywhere in the islands and also within Stanley Credit Card, and US dollars are also often accepted.
Credit cards from overseas islands are likely not accepted, although British, European, and American currencies can be used; obtain prior information from the owners to confirm the acceptable method of payment.
It is almost impossible to exchange the currency of the Falkland Islands outside the islands, so exchange your money before leaving the islands.
Since Montevideo is located in the Southern Hemisphere, it has summer when the Northern Hemisphere has winter, and vice versa.
